\title{10 · Adversarial review and current disposition — revision 1}
\taxon{Chapter}
\meta{origin}{design/10-adversarial-review.md}
\meta{layer}{human}
\tag{chapter}

\p{The original review and dispositions remain verbatim in \code{history/v0/10-adversarial-review.md}. This revision responds to the subsequent twelve-finding design review. A disposition below records a design change, not a proved Lean theorem. Required evidence is in \ref{ms-foundation}.}
\table{
  \tr{\th{Finding}\th{Current design response}\th{Remaining evidence}}
  \tr{\td{R1: horizontal bijectivity in DK clauses}\td{Remove that condition; require fixed-boundary cell faithfulness and simultaneous essential surjectivity}\td{\ref{at-fd-0005}; ∞-predicate and comparisons remain provisional}}
  \tr{\td{R2: relative maps lose natural equivalences}\td{Separate \code{MapRel}/\code{MapCat} and \code{VertRaw}/\code{VertCore}; retain vertical 2-cells}\td{\ref{at-fd-0004} and \ref{at-fd-0008}}}
  \tr{\td{R3: boundary monodromy invalidates hP}\td{Remove generic hP and its mandatory proof route; work coherently}\td{\ref{at-fd-0006}; optional specific truncations later}}
  \tr{\td{R4: contractible object values}\td{Require a reduced presentation and prove actual boundary/core lemmas}\td{\ref{at-fd-0003}}}
  \tr{\td{R5: Mat universes}\td{Raise collection universes; keep category object/hom parameters separate}\td{\ref{at-fd-0001}, no signatures compiled in this revision}}
  \tr{\td{R6: walking/slice fibres omit structure labels}\td{Fix entire selected monads/cones through relative diagram fibres}\td{\ref{at-fd-0008}, full \ref{at-up-0003}}}
  \tr{\td{R7: augmented active-chain encoding}\td{Replace the universal active-chain assertion with explicit augmented algebra/arity work}\td{\ref{at-fd-0007}, a material research risk}}
  \tr{\td{R8: BMW hypotheses conflated}\td{Separate arity recognition, pattern, and Reedy theorems}\td{\ref{at-fd-0007} and \ref{at-kr-0002}}}
  \tr{\td{R9: symmetric/braided monads on Mat}\td{Move to the profunctor ambient and retain permutation/braid morphisms}\td{\ref{at-fd-0009}; full ∞-construction \ref{ms-0007}}}
  \tr{\td{R10: independently opaque data and laws}\td{Bundle the specification with its laws, or prove an audited alternative}\td{\ref{at-fd-0002}}}
  \tr{\td{R11: broad rectification and paste promises}\td{State model changes and fixed-target scope separately; distinguish equality from coherent comparisons}\td{\ref{at-fd-0010}}}
  \tr{\td{R12: freeze before decisive tests}\td{Add \ref{ms-foundation}; move speculative infrastructure later; audit all axioms and both builds before merge}\td{\ref{at-fd-0011} and \ref{ms-foundation} exit}}
}
\p{The review's R3 claim is intentionally addressed conservatively: the faulty canonical transport argument is removed, without claiming that no useful homotopy equipment can exist. R4 identifies an invalid gluing justification; the proposed reduced replacement still needs a proof. R7 rejects a complete encoding by ordinary active chains; flagged augmented rows remain a possible richer presentation if their theorem is established. R10 does not say opaque interfaces are impossible: the revision uses data and laws in one specification, which is the appropriate prototype to test.}
\p{Earlier review findings about usable APIs, size, coherent choices, limits/colimits, span diagrams, invariance, duality, and interface growth remain relevant. Their prior “disposed” labels do not mean that the necessary ∞-theorems were proved. The current charter requires construction-specific certificates and treats failed gates as reasons to revise the mathematics.}
